  "_comment": "Sky presets for `python3 art/build.py sky <id>` (art/blender/common/sky.py DEFAULTS lists every key). STYLE_BIBLE 'Look rules' + tokens.json grade.maps.<tokens> own the numbers: sun_bearing_deg / sun_elevation_deg are the bible's compass numbers verbatim (0 = -Z north = screen-up, 90 = +X east, 180 = +Z toward the camera); air / aerosol / ozone / altitude_m are the Multiple Scattering densities from tokens.json. Sun disc OFF (the renderer's directional light is the sun), clouds live in the dome only (no cloud shadows), brightness normalised to a cos-weighted mean sky radiance of 1.0 (the renderer scales it by `ambient` = environmentIntensity). `out` is relative to art/out; `tokens` names the tokens.json map whose lighting/fog the build copies into lighting.json next to the HDR.",
